> convexity x^3
convexity of x^3:
  neither convex nor concave on all real x
    x in (-inf, 0]: concave (f'' < 0)
    x in [0, inf): convex (f'' > 0)
  inflection points: x = 0
  witness: f(-1) = -1 > (f(-2) + f(0))/2 = -4
  proved symbolically: f'' = 6x, a polynomial; its sign changes only at real roots of odd multiplicity
> convexity x^4
convexity of x^4:
  convex on all real x
  proved symbolically: f'' = 12x^2, a polynomial; its sign changes only at real roots of odd multiplicity
> convexity sin(x) in 0..6
convexity of sin(x):
  neither convex nor concave on [0, 6]
    x in [0, 3.141592654 (~pi)]: concave (f'' < 0)
    x in [3.141592654 (~pi), 6]: convex (f'' > 0)
  inflection points: x = 3.141592654 (~pi)
  witness: f(1.570796327) = 1 > (f(0) + f(3.141592654))/2 = 6.123233996e-17
  checked numerically, grid of 20001 points, sign of f''
> convexity abs(x)
convexity of abs(x):
  convex on [-10, 10]
  checked numerically on [-10, 10] (x has no range; give it one), sign of the second difference
> convexity 1/x
convexity of 1/x:
  neither (its domain is not an interval) on [-10, 10]
    x in [-10, -0.001]: concave (f'' < 0)
    x in [0.001, 10]: convex (f'' > 0)
  checked numerically on [-10, 10] (x has no range; give it one), sign of f''
> convex exp(x)
convexity of exp(x):
  convex on [-10, 10]
  checked numerically on [-10, 10] (x has no range; give it one), sign of f''
> concave -x^2
convexity of -x^2:
  concave on all real x
  proved symbolically: f'' = -2, a polynomial; its sign changes only at real roots of odd multiplicity
